From: Devin <devin@cognition.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: cover WAN LRO rings in RX IRQ2 bank

Adapted from orangeyoo/XR1710G-OpenWrt-iStoreOS-Community
9999-30-net-airoha-wan-lro-rx-irq-coverage.

The QDMA1 (WAN) RX IRQ2 bank pin mask is 0, so LRO rings 5, 21 and 22
are acknowledged by no IRQ bank on the WAN QDMA and aggregated WAN
flows landing on them stall.  Pin exactly those three rings to IRQ2,
which is otherwise unused, and assert at build time that the shared
LRO ring set is fully covered and not double-mapped.

Signed-off-by: Devin <devin@cognition.ai>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ static struct dentry *airoha_eth_dbgfs_d
 /* QDMA1 uses a different RX IRQ bank layout than QDMA0 on AN7581. */
 #define AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ0_BANK_PIN_MASK 0x0000839f
 #define AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ1_BANK_PIN_MASK 0x7f800400
-#define AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ2_BANK_PIN_MASK 0x00000000
+#define AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ2_BANK_PIN_MASK (BIT(5) | BIT(21) | BIT(22))
 #define AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ3_BANK_PIN_MASK 0x00000040
 
 static unsigned int airoha_qdma0_rx_irq_bank_mask[AIROHA_MAX_NUM_IRQ_BANKS] = {
@@ -724,6 +724,18 @@ static void airoha_dev_lro_enable(struc
 	int qdma_id = qdma - &eth->qdma[0];
 	int i, lro_queue_index = 0;
 
+	/* LRO producers share the ring set on both QDMAs. */
+	BUILD_BUG_ON(AIROHA_RXQ_LRO_EN_MASK &
+		     ~(AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ0_BANK_PIN_MASK |
+		       AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ1_BANK_PIN_MASK |
+		       AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ2_BANK_PIN_MASK |
+		       AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ3_BANK_PIN_MASK));
+	/* A ring must not be acknowledged by two IRQ banks. */
+	BUILD_BUG_ON(AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ2_BANK_PIN_MASK &
+		     (AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ0_BANK_PIN_MASK |
+		      AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ1_BANK_PIN_MASK |
+		      AIROHA_QDMA_WAN_RX_IRQ3_BANK_PIN_MASK));
+
 	if (airoha_fe_lro_is_enabled(eth, qdma_id))
 		return;
 
